# KEBU ID — BUSINESS IDENTITY SYSTEM

Kebu ID is the permanent digital identity assigned to a business inside Kebu.

Kebu ID is not the user’s personal identity and is not the mechanism used to verify whether a user is eligible to join Kebu.

## Keep these systems separate

1. **Personal Account** — individual user (name, contact, country, languages, skills, profile, roles, eligibility status, security).
2. **User Eligibility Verification** — whether the individual may access restricted Kebu services. States: unverified | pending | verified | rejected | expired | suspended | manual_review. Never treat a business ID as proof of personal eligibility.
3. **Kebu ID** — business / org / startup / cooperative / nonprofit / institution / registered commercial activity. One unique public ID per business (e.g. `KEBU-SN-01-A7K92P`). Non-sequential, hard to enumerate. Internal PK = UUID.

## Purpose

Kebu ID connects the business across profile, founders/team, registration, documents, store, payments, K21, analytics, funding, reputation — one trusted identity, not disconnected merchant/store/funding profiles.

**Kebu ID** identifies the business. **KA Score** (see `kebu-ka-score.mdc`) measures how that business is developing. Do not invent KA Score numbers inside Kebu ID slices.

## Creation & levels (never display higher than backend confirms)

- Created when user starts informal profile, registers, connects existing company, coop, nonprofit, institution, or via gov integration.
- Level 1 Draft · Level 2 Kebu-verified · Level 3 Government-registered · Level 4 Enhanced DD

## Ownership

Multi-person roles (founder, cofounder, beneficial_owner, director, administrator, finance_manager, store_manager, developer, designer, employee, accountant, legal_representative, viewer). Server-side RBAC. No self-elevation via browser. Ownership %, invitations, removals, multi-person auth, full audit.

## Country modules

Country-specific legal structures/fields/docs — versioned modules; do not hard-code Senegal into the global core.

## Security

Server ownership checks · RBAC · private docs + signed URLs · audit · fraud flags · duplicate detection · rate limits · secure invites · reauth for sensitive actions · MFA where required · idempotent create. Public Kebu ID must not leak private records.

## Slice discipline

One vertical slice at a time. Slice 1 = draft business create + founder + audit + dashboard load. Do **not** implement government registration, stores, payments, team invites, verification upgrades, or KA Score in Slice 1.

KA Score comes only after real business records, roles, activity, store ops, and analytics exist — and only when that slice is assigned.
